From: ghidra_rh850 project
Subject: [PATCH] sim: v850: implement RH850 synchronization instructions

RH850 firmware uses SYNCI after copying executable code and SYNCP before
publishing it.  sim/v850 currently treats both encodings as illegal
instructions, even though the simulator has no instruction/data-cache model
that needs additional state changes.

Decode SYNCI and SYNCP as completed synchronization operations.  This lets the
simulator execute the exact firmware bytes instead of requiring callers to
rewrite the instructions to NOPs.

Pinned base: GDB 6a5e5259790e5a854ddbb69eb486b9245fcfeee8
(gdb-18.1-release).
---
 sim/v850/v850.igen | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sim/v850/v850.igen b/sim/v850/v850.igen
index bd8de8e279..0000000000 100644
--- a/sim/v850/v850.igen
+++ b/sim/v850/v850.igen
@@ -1368,3 +1368,27 @@
+// SYNCI
+0000000000011100:I:::synci
+*v850e2
+*v850e2v3
+*v850e3v5
+"synci"
+{
+  /* The simulator has no instruction-cache state to invalidate.  */
+}
+
+
+
+// SYNCP
+0000000000011111:I:::syncp
+*v850e2
+*v850e2v3
+*v850e3v5
+"syncp"
+{
+  /* The scalar simulator completes all memory accesses in order.  */
+}
+
+
+
 // NOT
 rrrrr,000001,RRRRR:I:::not
 "not r<reg1>, r<reg2>"
